<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  What the app itself (Contents/MacOS/<main>) may ask macOS for under the hardened runtime, and nothing else.
  host/scripts/sign-mac.sh signs the app with it; the core and the speech helper get no entitlements at all, and
  host/scripts/check-signed.sh fails a bundle in which any program carries other than its own.

  - The microphone: hold to talk and Appearance's trial record in the app's web view, and macOS counts that as the
    app's. A program run in one of Tasktap's terminals is also counted as Tasktap's, as in any terminal app.
  - Apple Events: a program or an agent run in one of Tasktap's terminals (osascript, `tell application …`) is counted
    as Tasktap's too; without this, macOS refuses it without asking. Info.plist says why when macOS asks.

  Left out on purpose: the camera, contacts, calendars, photos and location (a program in a terminal that asks for
  one is refused), and every code-signing exception (JIT, unsigned memory, library validation, DYLD variables):
  the web view's JIT runs in WebKit's own processes, and every program in the bundle is plain compiled code.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
